<title>INDIA: Indian oil demand seen up 50 pct by 2001/2 - IOC.</title>
<headline>Indian oil demand seen up 50 pct by 2001/2 - IOC.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's oil consumption will rise by 50 percent by the year 2001/2, the Indian Oil Corporation (IOC) said on Monday.  </p>
<p>IOC chairman R.K. Narang told a meeting of shareholders that oil demand was expected to rise to 113 million tonnes by 2001/2 from 75 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>He said demand by the year 2006/7 was seen rising to 155 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
